       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/2961919de700a07ec22a098da2a90a31?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FMD-0.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Michael Durbin",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a45f9889d5006a6c0384",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Some things that immediately come to mind in the walk through include:",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "1.  Determining the disposition of your FOXML files",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "If Fedora 3 is still running AND actively being updated, they shouldn't point to the foxml directories.  If fedora will not be updated at all, maybe inform them about the id-resolution cache that will safe time on subsequent runs.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "They'll need to find out (from their fedora 3 configuration) whether they're using legacy or akubra storage and configure appropriately.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "2.  Determine how things should look in the fedora 4 repository.  ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Tell them where to set the URL. ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "Tell them about the pidmapper, how to configure the default, and how they may wish to write their own.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
