      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Some things that immediately come to mind in the walk through include:</p>\n\n<p>1.  Determining the disposition of your FOXML files<br/>\n  If Fedora 3 is still running AND actively being updated, they shouldn't point to the foxml directories.  If fedora will not be updated at all, maybe inform them about the id-resolution cache that will safe time on subsequent runs.<br/>\n  They'll need to find out (from their fedora 3 configuration) whether they're using legacy or akubra storage and configure appropriately.</p>\n\n<p>2.  Determine how things should look in the fedora 4 repository.  <br/>\nTell them where to set the URL. <br/>\nTell them about the pidmapper, how to configure the default, and how they may wish to write their own.</p>\n\n\n",
     "created": "07/May/15 1:11 PM",
     "id": "14233",
     "jsdPublic": true,
